{
  "schemaVersion": "lego.part-identification-truth-labels/1",
  "truth": "scripts/fixtures/part-identification-truth-first50.json",
  "note": "Binds each verdict of the first-fifty truth to the count label whose crop was judged. The judged crops are the files of the ignored run output/callout-thumbnails/runs/1e37c50ffee4df7741ac6722, each named p<page>-q<count>-x<x>-y<y>.png after the pdf.js position of its count label; the SHA-256 of every file listed here equals its verdict's judgedCropSha256, and all 84 verdict digests were found (verdict 25's crop bytes occur at two labels). A row carries no verdict, element or pixel: the verdict stays in the truth file, joined by n and checked by digest.",
  "errataNote": "Errata are verdicts the truth file gets wrong as element identities. The raters judged shape only, and an element id fixes colour as well as shape. Each erratum names the element the verdict claimed, the element the evidence supports, and the evidence: median ink colour of the callout and of both inventory thumbnails, as cut by apps/web/src/instructions/identify on booklet sha256:baef0a373164b58d7c982984b52d4e50b10cc59ed28007acb456faa72359bd27, and the inventory counts. scripts/identify-booklet.mjs still counts these as misses and prints the erratum beside each.",
  "errata": [
    {
      "n": 16,
      "claimed": "4210678",
      "correct": "383228",
      "reason": "shape-only verdict; the callout is the green 2x10 plate 383228, not the grey 4210678",
      "evidence": "callout p15 step 11 ink median RGB 48,159,86 (green); inventory 383228 median 48,150,85 (green); inventory 4210678 median 101,102,102 (dark bluish grey). 4210678 has inventory count 2, spent by the two byte-identical grey callouts on p85 (steps 96 and 98, median 105,105,106); 383228 has count 1. The verdict note itself says the colours differ."
    },
    {
      "n": 82,
      "claimed": "4210690",
      "correct": "6595205",
      "reason": "shape-only verdict; the callout is the dark blue 1x1x5 column 6595205, not the grey 4210690",
      "evidence": "callout p50 step 49 ink median RGB 34,62,104 (dark blue); inventory 6595205 median 34,62,102 (dark blue); inventory 4210690 median 106,106,106 (grey). The p50 drawing is byte-identical at the same size to the p53 drawing that verdict 83 judges to be 6595205. 6595205 has count 6 = p50 (3) + p53 (2) + p189 (1); 4210690 has count 3, spent by the grey drawing on p55, p191 and p212. The verdict note itself says the colours differ."
    }
  ],
